      "last_decision": {
        "at": "2026-10-20T13:40:39.168541+00:00",
        "symbol": "GOOG",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Stay flat on GOOG.NAS. The dispute the committee preserved is real and unchanged: primary-verified Q2-26 facts show revenue +24%, operating income +30% with ~34% margin and Cloud operating income of $8.8B on $24.8B revenue with $513.9B backlog, yet H1 OCF-minus-capex compressed to ~$4.3B, Q2 capex ($44.9B) exceeded Q2 OCF ($39.1B), and June 2026 financing raised $49.6B net in common/preferred plus a $20.3B note issue and a $40B ATM against a 5.1% 10Y and 5.43% 30Y. The tape gives no edge: RSI ~48, negative MACD histogram, price on the 20/50-day, 333-351 band, ATR ~8. Earnings date remains socially sourced, outage scope unverified, and the Q3 10-Q (the single number that settles Cloud operating income versus depreciation) is unfiled. Nothing new resolves the deferrals; hold into the print.",
        "thesis": "Watch stance carried forward: Alphabet's core engine is accelerating while the market prices unproven AI-capex ROI. Verified filings show durable demand (Cloud revenue $24.8B vs $13.6B y/y, segment operating income $8.8B, $513.9B Cloud backlog, Services operating income $39.5B) but also an equity/hybrid-funded buildout ($49.6B common/preferred net proceeds, $19.0B of 6.25% mandatory convertible preferred, capped calls, $40B ATM authorized) that converts balance-sheet strength into future share count and fixed charges. With a 5.1% 10Y, steep curve and oil/inflation backdrop compressing long-duration multiples, and an imminent earnings event able to clear the entire Bollinger band in one session given ATR ~2.5%, the neutral tape offers no directional edge. The decisive variable is Q3 Cloud segment operating income versus depreciation and any capex guidance revision, neither yet filed. Six hours is an ordinary minimum; the patient path is to wait for primary-filing resolution rather than pay for either hypothesis pre-print.",
        "countercase": "Bulls argue the bar is reset low after the ~6% post-Q2 drop despite 82% reported Cloud growth, margin expansion outruns rate drag, the 200-day (~339) held on Monday, debt is trivially serviceable against ~$130B annualized operating income, and backlog verifies contracted demand; staged pre-print exposure captures a re-rating that waiting forfeits. Bears counter that at 5.1% long yields, capex financed with equity and mandatory converts before ROI is proven is serial dilution; a soft Meta print on Oct 21 could de-rate the whole hyperscaler complex before Alphabet reports, and today's Google Cloud outage (two-feed corroborated, scope unverified) hands skeptics pre-earnings ammunition against the segment the thesis rests on. Both cases are credible; neither is confirmed by primary Q3 evidence, which is exactly why neither side should be paid for now.",
        "invalidation": "The watch stance resolves to action on specific events: (1) Q3-26 10-Q filing, verify Cloud segment operating income versus nearly doubled H1 depreciation ($9.5B to $13.6B), any capex guidance revision, and like-for-like backlog growth given the Q1-26 definition change that added <=1-year contracts; (2) confirmation of the earnings date via 8-K rather than social posts; (3) news verification of the Oct-20 Cloud outage scope, duration and any issuer statement; (4) Meta's Oct-21 print as the hyperscaler read-across; (5) price evidence: a decisive break below the 200-day (~339 on the dated series) on volume, or a range breakout above ~351 with Cloud-positive confirmation. A close would require an owned position whose thesis a new filing or verified event specifically invalidates; none exists yet. Full-filing certification remains incomplete, which the owner has authorized for demo but which further justifies no directional exposure before primary Q3 numbers.",
        "status": "approved",
